# Core patches are applied to a source tree byte for byte, so git must not touch their line
# endings. TGB Dual ships some sources with CRLF, so its patch carries CRLF in those hunks'
# context lines; normalised to LF on checkout it would no longer match the file it patches.
# The build refuses a patch set that changed nothing (cores/tgbdual/build.sh), so this failing
# would be loud rather than silent, but the point is for it not to fail.
cores/**/*.patch -text
